    "result_text": "That's a JaCoCo coverage exclusion (generated DTOs), not a test exclusion. The build is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's a summary of what I did to unify `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId`.\n\n## What changed\n\n**New identifier format** \u2014 `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (no separators), e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`:\n- **REGION** \u2014 region code from postcode/city (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`/`UNKNOWN`)\n- **FY** \u2014 2-digit fiscal-year segment of the business-day-adjusted registration date\n- **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` (the same hash the old customer code used)\n- **CHK** \u2014 one Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n\n## Files touched\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the stored `customerCode` field with `memberId` (`member_id` column); removed the stored `membershipNumber` field and the derived `getCheckDigit()`; rewrote `getLocality()` to recover the REGION prefix from `memberId` (via a known-region match, since segments are now delimiter-less). Kept the shared `luhnCheckDigit`/`fiscalYearSegment`/`sha256Hex` helpers.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `generateCustomerCode`/`generateMembershipNumber`/`deduplicateCustomerCode` with `generateMemberId`/`deduplicateMemberId`; collision handling (`-<n>` suffix) now applies to `memberId`; the audit line now logs `memberId`.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 the structured audit record's primary-identifier component is now `memberId`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit` schema properties; added `memberId`; updated the `locality` description. (DTO is regenerated and MapStruct wires `memberId` by name.)\n- **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`, dropped `membership_number`; updated the hsqldb positional seed inserts to match the new column count.\n\n## Verification\n\n`./mvnw -B test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` passes: the response exposes `memberId` starting with `NSW` and containing the computed HASH8, and no longer has `customerCode` or `membershipNumber`.",
